# CVE-2025-8194: cpython infinite loop in tarfile parsing (HIGH)
# Status: Pending fix in Debian 12 (bookworm) - CVE published 2025-08-XX
# Impact: DoS via infinite loop when parsing malicious tarfile
# Package: Python 3.11 standard library
# Mitigation:
#   - Input validation: File upload restricted to .xlsx, .csv, .json (NO tar files accepted)
#   - File type whitelist enforced in backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/import_endpoints.py
#   - Max file size limit: 50 MB (prevents large malicious archives)
# Risk assessment: LOW (tar uploads not supported)
# Next review: 2026-04-03 (quarterly check)
CVE-2025-8194

# CVE-2026-1299: cpython email header injection via unquoted newlines (HIGH)
# Status: Pending fix in Debian 12 (bookworm) - CVE published 2026-01-XX
# Impact: Email header injection allowing spam/phishing via unquoted newlines
# Package: Python 3.11 standard library (email module)
# Mitigation:
#   - Email sending via python-telegram-bot (NOT stdlib email module)
#   - User input sanitized before email generation (FastAPI validation)
#   - No direct user control over email headers
# Risk assessment: MEDIUM (email functionality exists, but controlled)
# Next review: 2026-03-03 (weekly check)
CVE-2026-1299

